# Who is asked to review what. See GOVERNANCE.md.
#
# Each project profile has one line. The maintainers own it. Do not leave a line
# with no owner: GitHub then treats the file as having no code owner at all.
#
# Profile reviewers are NOT listed here (GOVERNANCE.md, Profile reviewers).
# There are two kinds: a representative, who works on the project, and an
# external steward, who has no affiliation with any covered project and looks
# after the profile when no representative is interested. GitHub requires a code
# owner to have write access, and one code owner on a line is enough for GitHub.
# A code owner's approval would then count as the approval of the profile. So
# their reviews are requested by hand, recorded in the pull request, and listed
# in MAINTAINERS.md.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners of a file when a pull request is
# ready for review (not while it is a draft). Branch protection decides whether
# that review is required. When it is required, an approval from any one owner
# on the line is enough. GitHub ignores an owner with no write access to this
# repository.

*                                    @mauromorales

# Conflicted files (GOVERNANCE.md, "Conflict of interest"). The first maintainer
# who is not affiliated with Kairos or Hadron and is not employed by Spectro
# Cloud replaces @mauromorales on these lines as the required approver. Adding
# them next to @mauromorales would not make their approval required, because
# any one owner on a line is enough. GitHub enforces only that a code owner
# approves. The approver rule (the approver is not affiliated with any project
# that the author is affiliated with, and is not employed by any employer of
# the author) rests on the maintainers and the public record. data/lineage.yaml,
# site/projects_meta.yaml, site/content.py and site/drafts/base_choice.yaml
# state facts about Kairos, Hadron and Spectro Cloud next to facts about the
# other projects. GitHub cannot protect one entry of a file, so the whole file
# is listed. During the bootstrap, a change that touches an entry about Kairos,
# Hadron or Spectro Cloud is conflicted. This file, MAINTAINERS.md and
# CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md are listed so that the hand-over cannot be undone without
# the approval of the maintainer named on these lines. CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md names
# the enforcement contact. Any other file that states a fact about these
# projects counts the same way. site/build.py holds such labels and text, for
# example the Kairos fleet server name. It is code, so it is not listed here,
# and the rule still applies to it. GOVERNANCE.md holds the ownership,
# administrator and removal rules. A change to it is conflicted and follows all
# four rules, and for 24 months after the bootstrap ends the founder clause in
# it also needs the owner's agreement for the protected text in it.
